# Wayfinder efforts under .scratch/ are tracked as documents, but never the
# corpora they were measured against: those hold verbatim stakeholder text from
# a real institution's internal documents, and the source PDFs are large and
# publicly available elsewhere.
.scratch/**/eval/baseline/
.scratch/**/sources/

# Tooling state, not project work: installed skill bundles and their lockfile.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# The TCISM test set the scope-guard work was measured against. Same reason the
# .scratch corpora above are excluded: verbatim stakeholder text from one real
# institution's internal documents, plus that program's human-authored answer
# key. Referenced by .scratch/plo-scope-guard/ but never committed with it.
#
# Matched by basename, with no directory part on purpose. These were written as
# `Data/<name>` and the directory was later renamed to `references/`, which
# silently un-ignored both files — a rename is not supposed to be able to stage a
# corpus. A pattern without a slash matches at any depth, so the next move cannot
# do that either.
ความต้องการของผู้มีส่วนได้ส่วนเสีย การแป.docx
Needs_to_PLO_TCISM.xlsx
